--- body ---
## Context

Panel v1 ([[1895]], `data/jetp/reference/panel-v1/`, PR #1664) delivered
299 lines for USD 8.87 but is not conclusive (author, 2026-10-01): one
informative stratum (ZAF en prose span, 35 of 50 held-out lines from one
document); 66 of 836 aligned items unanimous (8 percent); 182 of 233 medium
lines with the third member absent. Diagnosis, from its README:

- **Text layer, not models.** A hand-built pdftotext layer and a
  contiguous-substring locator: `-layout` interleaved the Vietnamese
  newsletter columns; no text order recovers the wrapped-cell grants
  register. Members read correctly (reading order, logical rows) and the
  check rejected them. Same failure as the spike (22 of 28 misses were
  locator rejections).
- **Under-defined task.** 278 items proposed by one member only (members
  disagree on what one statement is); 185 same-span items split by
  classification; 74 field disagreements, mostly on five ad hoc panel
  fields (funder versus implementer) that are not the ontology's.
- **The ontology was not given.** Only the 13 line classifications reached
  the members; not the classes, relations and closed lists of
  `docs/jetp-ontology.md` and `data/jetp/ontology/`, against the author
  decision of [[1890]] ("never in a vacuum").

## Design (accepted shape, author 2026-10-01)

- **Layer: Docling**, not a hand-built adapter (survey
  `conception/jetp-m2-3-reading-design-survey-2026-10-01.md` picked it):
  reading order across columns, table cells as cells, a numbered element
  per block. Locator = element ID (page, table, row and cell for a table;
  block for prose), derived by code, as extraction § 5 already specifies.
  **Mistral OCR 4 is a reluctant fallback only** (not open weight): hosted
  under zero retention, for a document Docling reads badly or a scan, each
  use named in the record.
- **Readers point, they do not quote.** Members pick element IDs from the
  numbered layer; the ID and every closed list are schema enums, so a
  locator cannot fail to resolve and a value cannot leave its list. Hosted:
  JSON-schema structured output with `require_parameters`. Local:
  llama.cpp GBNF, or llguidance (`~/llama.cpp-new/build-llg`) where a
  verbatim substring must be constrained.
- **The ontology, all of it.** Classes, relations and closed value lists in
  force (`data/jetp/ontology/`), and the verbatim field list of each
  document type from the ontology, not invented fields.
- **The statement unit defined per shape before any run**: what one
  statement is for a table row, a record page and a prose span, with a
  classification decision rule for the confusable pairs seen in v1
  (named_item, register_allocation, envelope, heading).
- **Split by document**, not by line, so the held-out part measures unseen
  documents; draw weighted to the thin strata (VNM, SEN, IDN).
- Kept from v1: blind cross-vendor panel distinct from readers and arbiter,
  positive control first (made harder than v1's four items), versioned
  agreement rule committed before the first call, sealed held-out hash,
  the limit named (agreement with a panel, not truth).

## Spending gate

No paid call, hosted or Mistral OCR, before the author's explicit go on a
priced step (author, 2026-10-01). Local runs on padme need no budget but
are coordinated with any session holding the GPUs.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Docling layer for the v1 documents, its version pinned; the elements
  of the v1 grants register and one Vietnamese newsletter checked to come
  out as cells and in reading order
- [ ] Statement unit per shape and classification decision rule written
  and committed, with the full ontology prompt and schema
- [ ] Free agreement check before any spend: v1's kept answers re-scored
  where possible, and the defined unit applied to two documents locally (or
  by the cheapest hosted route once approved), unanimity reported against
  v1's 8 percent
- [ ] Priced pilot plan (2 documents, then the full draw) presented, and
  the author's go logged here before any paid call
- [ ] Panel v2 built: control passed, split by document and sealed, counts
  per stratum with the strata under 30 held-out items named, limit named
- [ ] [[1890]] records that v2 is its reference set, or why not
- [ ] Spec amended for the author's decision of 2026-10-01 dropping zero retention: `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 5 and § 7 (fail-closed rule) and `docs/jetp-legal-note.md` (what must change), the kept safeguards (data_collection deny, local_only) and the go-live legal review named; the panel client's zero-retention pin made a configurable setting
